    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5876" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφικέφᾰλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>two-headed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				107.10
			</span></i> (in poet. form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφικέφαλλος</span>); of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφίσβαινα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.243
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέλους τὸ ἀ.,</span> i.e. the
			thighbone, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				404a5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of a couch,
				<i>having two places for the head,</i> i.e. <i>two ends,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλίνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					1.277d
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κνέφαλλος</span> wrongly cited by
				<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				10.36
			</span></i>).</div>
